Subject: mariadb-java-client 3.5.11 in the Nessie Quarkus server
CVE: CVE-2026-119281
CVE: CVE-2026-119276
CVE: CVE-2026-119210
CVE: CVE-2026-119280
Origin: DHI-internal (Nessie Quarkus server dependency pin)
Description: Force org.mariadb.jdbc:mariadb-java-client to 3.5.11 in the Quarkus server, which the Quarkus platform BOM would otherwise resolve to 3.5.10.
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/projectnessie/nessie.git 261e936e2b72a130ebc5e3a10b8b1e9d55eb6872
Verify: sbom pkg:maven/org.mariadb.jdbc/mariadb-java-client@3.5.11
Forwarded: not-needed (dependency pin inside the DHI build; upstream keeps its own version in gradle/libs.versions.toml)
Drop-When: dependency org.mariadb.jdbc:mariadb-java-client >= 3.5.11
Regenerate: `apply the earlier nessie patches in pipeline order to the nessie-0.109.0 tree, add the mariadb force block after the guava block in servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts, then run git diff on that file`

The Quarkus platform BOM manages the MariaDB JDBC driver that quarkus-jdbc-mariadb pulls into the Nessie Quarkus server, and it still resolves 3.5.10 for the fast-jar packaging. Forcing the fixed release in the server build keeps the packaged jar and the SBOM at 3.5.11 so the scanner stops reporting the four MariaDB findings.

diff --git a/servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts b/servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts
--- a/servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts
+++ b/servers/quarkus-server/build.gradle.kts
@@ -41,6 +41,17 @@
   }
 }
 
+// CVE-2026-119281, CVE-2026-119276, CVE-2026-119210, CVE-2026-119280: the Quarkus platform BOM
+// still resolves mariadb-java-client 3.5.10 through quarkus-jdbc-mariadb. Force the fixed 3.5.11
+// release so the fast-jar packaging and the SBOM/Scout scan reflect the fixed version.
+configurations.configureEach {
+  resolutionStrategy {
+    force(
+      "org.mariadb.jdbc:mariadb-java-client:3.5.11",
+    )
+  }
+}
+
 // CVE-2026-54291 (GHSA-j92g-9f8w-j867): pgjdbc SCRAM-SHA-256-PLUS channel binding downgrade,
 // fixed in 42.7.12. The Quarkus platform BOM can still constrain pgjdbc to 42.7.11,
 // so force the resolved jar to 42.7.12 so the fast-jar packaging and the SBOM/Scout scan
